  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol D3 is shown to have a target relationship with U373 MG through multiple pathways, all of which involve the compound interacting with SNU-387, a molecule that is subsequently targeted by U373 MG. The evidence suggests that Certonardosterol D3 may act as a modulator of SNU-387, which in turn influences U373 MG. The presence of multiple distinct molecular structures that are all targeted by U373 MG, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and Dendocarbin K, indicates that the compound may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving distinct binding sites or pathways. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a potential role for Certonardosterol D3 in targeting U373 MG through the modulation of SNU-387, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action.",
